NanoLLM loads the following third-party components at runtime. They are not
compiled into the binary; release archives carry them in lib/ together with
their licence texts.

  llama.cpp   MIT   https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
  ggml        MIT   https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml
              lib/libllama*, lib/libggml*, lib/llama.dll, lib/ggml*.dll and
              the Metal shaders, from the pinned llama.cpp release; the
              licence text is below.

  LLVM OpenMP runtime   Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
              https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/tree/main/openmp
              Windows archives only: lib/libomp.dll, which the clang-cl
              builds of ggml link. Full text: lib/LICENSE-LLVM-OpenMP.

  NVIDIA CUDA runtime and cuBLAS   NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit EULA
              https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/
              CUDA add-on archives only (*-cuda.*): lib/libcudart*,
              lib/libcublas*, cudart64*.dll, cublas64*.dll, cublasLt64*.dll,
              redistributed unmodified as the EULA's Attachment A permits,
              together with ggml-cuda from the same llama.cpp release.

Go dependencies compiled into the binary:

  gopkg.in/yaml.v3              MIT and Apache-2.0   https://github.com/go-yaml/yaml
  github.com/ebitengine/purego  Apache-2.0           https://github.com/ebitengine/purego
  golang.org/x/sys              BSD-3-Clause         https://cs.opensource.google/go/x/sys
  modernc.org/sqlite, libc,     BSD-3-Clause         https://gitlab.com/cznic
    mathutil, memory

Model weights are NOT part of this repository or of any release archive and
carry their own licences. Each catalog entry records its licence, and from
v1.0 registry.strict_license refuses weights not licensed for commercial use.

